nication issues. C has reliability and decision quality but lacks stress and technical data, also communication issues. So B seems best. As Agent 1, we can align with B, perhaps note that while B's communication concerns are serious, they may be mitigated, and no other candidate has documented reliability and stress resilience. So we can keep vote for B.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: Agent 3's argument, Agent 2's support, and our own earlier info that we lack reliability and stress data for A and D. Use explicit facts: B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Also note B's communication issues (nasty remarks) but compare to C's communication difficulty and egocentric, and D's arrogance, A's unorganized and poor criticism acceptance. So B still best.\n\nThus public message: I agree with Agent 3, keep B as provisional lead, because B's documented reliability and stress resilience are critical, and other candidates lack those data. I note that B's communication issues remain a risk but can be addressed.\n\nVote: Candidate B.\n\nNow produce output."}
